  "graph_id": "mirofish_local_984d8a714a584639",
  "simulation_requirement": "Predict the public sentiment, social media reaction, and institutional reputation impact following the rollout of DBS Bank's targeted initiative to cap daily withdrawal limits at $7,000 for Work Permit Holder (WPH) accounts.\r\n\r\nContext & Inputs:\r\nDBS Background & Context.pdf: Use this to establish the institutional baseline, existing anti-scam frameworks, and regulatory standing.\r\n\r\nDBS Anti-Scam Initiatives for Work Permit Holders.pdf: Contains the existing initiatives/measures against scams for work permit holders.\r\n\r\nSimulation Objectives:\r\nEvaluate whether the public perceives this as a proactive security measure (protecting the vulnerable) or institutional discrimination (unfairly targeting a specific demographic).\r\n\r\nSimulate how the narrative evolves from the affected user base to the broader digital public square.\r\n\r\nDetermine the tipping point where this operational friction becomes a viral reputational issue.\r\n\r\nOutput Requirements:\r\nPlease provide the final report in the following format:\r\n\r\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY: Majority perception, binary verdict: Positive/Negative/Neutral, and key inflection points.\r\n\r\nTEMPORAL SENTIMENT TRENDS: The lifecycle of the reaction from initial notice to widespread discourse.\r\n\r\nGRANULAR CLUSTER ANALYSIS: How the sentiment diverges between different groups.\r\n\r\nSTRATEGIC ACTION ITEMS: Risk mitigation steps for the bank to address the friction without compromising the anti-scam objective.\"",
